  "dots_index_lines": [
    "## Dots",
    "- [Meet dots](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots.md): An always-on agent that keeps work moving and asks for your input when a decision needs you.",
    "- [Connect computers and apps to your dot](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/computers-and-apps.md): Use your dot's cloud computer, connect your own computer, and manage app access.",
    "- [Control your dot](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/controls.md): Review work, set custom rules, manage permissions, and stop or delete your dot.",
    "- [Get started with your dot](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/getting-started.md): Set up your dot and learn how to work with it over time.",
    "- [Message your dot](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/channels.md): Message or call your dot in ChatGPT, and connect other contact methods.",
    "- [Tasks and memory](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/tasks-and-memory.md): Understand assigned work, recurring tasks, and your dot's context",
    "- [Local computer access for Work Cloud and dots](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/cloud-local-access.md): Review shared policies and compatibility, then enable local computer access separately for Work and dots"
  ],
